-- so the count is not a function of the molecule, for a second reason independent of the first. Glycerol
-- showed the medium deciding; cyclohexane shows the timescale deciding, on a molecule with no stereocentre
-- and no enantiotopic pair anywhere in it. Both are the same statement: the group is a function of the
-- motions and the setting, and the identity of the molecule does not carry it.
cyh-counts-differ : signals-under 18 cyh-warm cyh-h nmr-achiral ≡ signals-under 18 cyh-cold cyh-h nmr-achiral → Empty
cyh-counts-differ q = transport (λ i → isTrue (eqb 1 ((concat (sym cyh-warm-count) (concat q cyh-cold-count)) i))) unit
